            <ArticleTitle>Plasma pyridoxal-5-phosphate level as risk index for coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Preliminary evidence is presented that plasma pyridoxal-5-phosphate levels are considerably and significantly reduced (P less than 0.0001) in patients suffering from myocardial infarction when compared to a healthy control group.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
